  "body": "## What changed\n\n### New `mcc-help` command\n\n`mcc-help` (legacy alias `fcc-help`) prints a command reference covering every native command, how each is used, the legacy `fcc-*` aliases, and the install-while-running / restart behavior. Registered in `[project.scripts]` and the identity owner map, so `--version` resolves the right owner.\n\n```\nMy Claude Code -- commands\n\nStart the proxy:\n  mcc-server              Start the local proxy and admin dashboard\n  my-claude-code          Same as mcc-server (full command name)\n\nUse a coding agent through the proxy:\n  mcc-claude              Launch Claude Code through the proxy\n  mcc-claude --discover-models   Also enable the model picker from the catalog\n  mcc-claude-old          Legacy launcher: full proxy environment, auto-compact\n  mcc-codex               Launch Codex through the proxy\n  mcc-pi                  Launch Pi through the proxy\n\nManage and inspect:\n  mcc-init                Create or repair ~/.fcc/.env with the config template\n  mcc-chatgpt-oauth-login Log in to ChatGPT/Codex via OAuth device flow\n  mcc-compact-log         Compact the request log (deduplicate + compress)\n  mcc-help                Show this command reference\n...\n```\n\n### Installers lead with mcc commands\n\nBoth installers' post-install message now:\n- leads with the `mcc-*` commands and what each does;\n- mentions `mcc-help`;\n- notes the legacy `fcc-*` commands remain as aliases;\n- includes the restart note (\"restart the proxy with: mcc-server\").\n\nThe POSIX/WSL path is unchanged: install-while-running works, and the new version is picked up on the next `mcc-server` restart.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Real WSL install (isolated home) of the LF `install.sh`: installs, verifies `fcc-server --version`, prints the new mcc message.\n- `mcc-help` output covers every native command (unit test asserts each is present).\n- `ruff`/`ty` clean. Full suite: **16 failed / 3662 passed** — identical failure set to unmodified main (16 pre-existing PowerShell failures), zero regressions.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The `mcc-help` text is hand-maintained; the unit test asserts every native command appears but not that descriptions stay accurate if command behavior changes. A future guard could cross-check the launcher docstrings.\n- The legacy `fcc-*` commands remain fully functional aliases; they are acknowledged (not advertised) in the help and install messages.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
