    "message": "feat: 5.1.0 add mcc-help command and lead installers with mcc commands\n\nNew capability: `mcc-help` (legacy alias `fcc-help`) prints a command reference\ncovering every native command, how each is used, the legacy fcc-* aliases, and\nthe install-while-running / restart behavior. Registered in [project.scripts]\nand the identity owner maps, so `--version` resolves the right owner.\n\nBoth installers' post-install message now leads with the mcc command family and\ndescribes each command (start the proxy, use a coding agent, manage/inspect),\nmentions `mcc-help`, and notes the legacy fcc-* commands remain as aliases plus\nthe restart note. The POSIX/WSL path is unchanged: install while running works,\nand the new version is picked up on the next `mcc-server` restart.\n\nVerified: real WSL install (isolated home) of the LF install.sh installs\nv5.0.3, verifies fcc-server --version, and prints the new mcc message. ruff/ty\nclean. Full suite 16 failed / 3662 passed -- identical failure set to\nunmodified main (16 pre-existing PowerShell failures), zero regressions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
